BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a418e47b2c2d9043@role-civil-litigation-appellate.maine-government-feeds
DTSTAMP:20260826T200218Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260826
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] Attorney General Aaron M. Frey Sues United St
 ates Postal Service Over Unlawful Attempt to Interfere with States’ Vote
 -by-Mail Procedures
DESCRIPTION:FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE\nContact: Danna Hayes\,\nDanna.hayes@mai
 ne.gov\nAttorney General Aaron M. Frey Sues United States Postal Service O
 ver Unlawful Attempt to Interfere with States’ Vote-by-Mail Procedures\n
 Lawsuit Seeks to Block Unconstitutional USPS Rule that Directs States to O
 verhaul Vote-by-Mail Procedures on an Impossible Timeline and Risks Disenf
 ranchising Eligible Voters\nAUGUSTA –\nAttorney General Aaron M. Frey to
 day joined a coalition of 25 states in filing a lawsuit against the United
  States Postal Service (USPS) challenging its new rule that purports to gr
 ant USPS the authority to regulate mail voting in elections.\nTens of mill
 ions of voters across the country rely on mail-in ballots\, and the coalit
 ion argues USPS’s rule will prevent states from effectively administerin
 g their mail voting programs\, putting voters at risk of being disenfranch
 ised.\n“USPS and the President are inflicting violence on free and fair 
 elections through this unlawful attempt to control voting by mail\, said\n
 Attorney General Frey\n. “This is not hard: the Constitution\ndoes not\n
 trust the Executive Branch with the responsibility of facilitating electio
 ns and this new rule – this election interference – must be stopped.
 ”\nOn March 31\, President Trump issued an Executive Order attempting to
  establish a national list of eligible voters and directing the U.S. Posta
 l Service to transmit mail ballots only to voters on the list. On August 2
 1\, USPS announced a new rule implementing the President’s demands that 
 require states to register every voter who is eligible to vote by mail wit
 h USPS and tasking USPS with compiling the registered voters into state-sp
 ecific lists. The rule also establishes new design requirements for the ma
 il-in ballot envelopes created by states\, which states are required to me
 et and get approved by USPS. Under the rule\, USPS will not deliver ballot
 s to voters who do not appear on the USPS-generated lists and will not del
 iver ballots in envelopes that fail to comply with the \nhttps://www.maine
 .gov/ag/news-and-library/press-releases/attorney-general-aaron-m-frey-sues
 -united-states-postal-service
URL:https://www.maine.gov/ag/news-and-library/press-releases/attorney-gene
 ral-aaron-m-frey-sues-united-states-postal-service
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
